---
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="memory" first="gone" title="Write it down" description="The window is emptied between sessions. A short instruction file in the project is loaded at the start of every one.">
  <Step id="gone" title="The window does not outlive the session">
    <p>The new <Term id="thread" /> from <LessonRef id="window" /> starts empty, like every chat since <LessonRef id="chat" />. That clears the clutter, and also everything the agent worked out yesterday.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="file" title="A short file in your project does">
    <ForLevel is="plain">
      <p><code>AGENTS.md</code> is an <Term id="instructions" />: plain text in your project folder, the green tile. The tool loads it before your first message, so your date format and style rules are there every time.</p>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="technical">
      <p><code>AGENTS.md</code> loads into every new session before your prompt. Put the test runner, the check command (<code>npm run check</code>, which runs <code>tsc --noEmit</code> and <code>vitest run</code>) and the folder layout there, so it never guesses.</p>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="engineer">
      <p><code>AGENTS.md</code> loads into every new session before your prompt. Record stack decisions, module boundaries, the verify command and the shortcuts that are not allowed; leave tutorials out.</p>
    </ForLevel>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="session" data-val="with" data-default aria-pressed="true">With AGENTS.md</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="session" data-val="without" aria-pressed="false">Without</button>
    </div>
    <More title="Which file each tool reads">
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.contextFile" show="claim" /></p>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.codex.contextFile" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="grow" title="Add a rule when a mistake repeats">
    <p>Tell it to add one short line when it gets something wrong twice. Keep pressing, and watch what a long file does to the next job.</p>
    <div class="row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-do="teach">Add a rule</button></div>
    <ForLevel is="plain">
      <More title="A prompt for this">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Add a plain rule to AGENTS.md">{`You wrote the date as month/day. This project uses day.month.year everywhere.\nAdd one short line to AGENTS.md so every future session knows. Show me the line first.`}</CopyPrompt>
        <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.claudeMdLines" show="claim" /></p>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="technical">
      <More title="Starter AGENTS.md for tests & types">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Technical AGENTS.md skeleton">{`# Project rules\n- Tests: vitest, run with npm test (not jest).\n- Before reporting done, run: npm run check (tsc --noEmit && vitest run).\n- Add a unit test for every bug fix and pure logic change.`}</CopyPrompt>
        <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.claudeMdLines" show="claim" /></p>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="engineer">
      <More title="Starter AGENTS.md for architecture & stack">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Engineer AGENTS.md skeleton">{`# Architecture & verification\n- Stack: strict TypeScript, Vite, Vitest. Zero unapproved runtime deps.\n- Boundaries: pure domain logic in src/domain/ (no DOM or DB imports); UI reads via typed selectors.\n- Done means: npm run check (tsc --noEmit && vitest run && lint) passes before any commit or PR.`}</CopyPrompt>
        <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.claudeMdLines" show="claim" /></p>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
  </Step>
  <Step id="skills" title="Skills wait on the shelf until needed">
    <p>A <a href={url('wiki/skill/')} data-side>skill</a> is a checklist for one kind of job, such as making a PDF. Only its name and one line sit in the window; the rest loads when a job needs it.</p>
    <div class="row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-do="skill">Ask for a PDF</button></div>
    <Next from="memory" more={[{ href: 'wiki/instruction-file/', text: 'Instruction files', side: true }, { href: 'library/', text: 'Browse starter skills in the Library' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The jobs, the rules and the line numbers are made up.</p>
    <Verified ids={['harnesses.claudeCode.contextFile', 'harnesses.codex.contextFile', 'harnesses.claudeCode.claudeMdLines']} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
